---
title: Ladder Storage
hidden: false
---
Ladder Storage is a glitch discovered in 2024 by [Eloise](https://www.youtube.com/@eloelo__) that allows the player to lock their character's stable position to the top or bottom of a ladder.

The glitch is performed by riposting or backstabbing an enemy while simultaneously climbing the ladder on the exact same frame. Once this state is achieved, any of the following actions will break the ladder storage: pivoting, quitting out, running out of stamina, getting staggered, triggering the fall animation, or climbing another ladder.

Ladder Storage has a few practical applications. It can be used to perform an action elsewhere in the game and then quit out, causing the player to respawn back at the ladder, as shown in [this clip](https://youtu.be/xy009H76VXA?t=2078).

It can also be used to perform a *ladder warp*, a far more complex glitch explained in [this video](https://youtu.be/1hACzV8Ye1I) by Catalystz. The ladder warp has found use in the Any% console route for *Dark Souls Remastered*.

\
Note that this glitch is used much more in the original version of Dark Souls than in the Remastered version

## **External resources**

Tutorial on how to perform this glitch [https://youtu.be/E9IdKMAqra0](https://youtu.be/E9IdKMAqra0) by Eloise on Youtube.
